# Example: KDE Plasma global shortcut for sayit (toggle mode)
# Add it in System Settings -> Shortcuts -> Custom Shortcuts,
# or set it programmatically with kwriteconfig5/kwriteconfig6.
#
# Shortcut: Meta+D (or any free key, e.g. F12)
# Command:  $HOME/path/to/sayit/bin/sayit
#
# Manual installation via shell:
#
# kwriteconfig6 --file kglobalshortcutsrc \
#     --group "sayit" \
#     --key "_k_friendly_name" "sayit"
#
# kwriteconfig6 --file kglobalshortcutsrc \
#     --group "sayit" \
#     --key "toggle" "Meta+D,none,Start/stop dictation"
#
# Then wire it up via the kglobalaccel D-Bus interface, or create a .desktop
# file under ~/.local/share/applications/sayit.desktop (template in
# config/sayit.desktop) and bind it in System Settings -> Shortcuts.
